# Post-Change Rules & Docs Check

After completing any non-trivial code change, review whether the change affects the accuracy of existing project documentation or cursor rules.

Check:
- `.cursor/rules/` — do any rules describe behavior that has changed or constraints that no longer hold?
- `docs/` — docs covering architecture, API conventions, or module structure

If stale content exists, update it in the same session as the code change. If no updates are needed, no action is required — the check is a prompt to look, not a requirement to write.
